    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d457-a1">

                <pb facs="1745" n="1640" xml:id="pg1640"/>


                <head>Memorandum From Gray to Goodpaster</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1959-04-09">April 9, 1959</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d457-3" n="3" type="facsimile" xml:id="d457-3"/>
                <p>You no doubt have copies of this further exchange of correspondence. However,
                    please note Mr. Herter’s statement about having informed the President.</p>
                <p>Do you think that the President is sufficiently informed about the potential
                    serious difference of view in this matter? I agree with Mr. McCone that there
                    may be a great difference between a system of “deterrents” and a system
                    providing adequate inspection and control.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Gordon Gray</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Special Assistant to the President</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
